 "committedCopy": "THE RUN THAT WENT RED FOR THE WRONG REASON. An independent critic re-ran the package's own documented sabotage on a busy laptop on 2026-09-20 and it came back FAIL --same 0.05%, exit 1, 'the sabotage moved 5 of 5 (pose, regime) frames past --same' -- and verdict.uninterpretable was EMPTY, every frame camera ok and settled, both sides 196 buildings and 2,600,942 triangles, identical grade. Then they opened the frames: side A, the UNSABOTAGED control, was the broken one. Its tree canopies were bright unretinted green under a night sky, the authored towers' lit window grids were absent (windows.pct 3.371% against 13.349% for the same pose, regime and build in the kept baseline), and at capitol/congress-30m the Capitol dome is MISSING from A and present in B. The diff image is dominated by A's defect, not by B's sabotage: the two Capitol poses read 3.354% and 1.117% here against 0.025% and 0.002% in same-break-apartments.report.json at the same poses. The only trace anywhere in the report was tilesOk:false on all five A shots against tilesOk:true on all five B shots -- a field that was recorded per shot and then never reached verdict, the summary or the exit code. Both sides took 2 reloads and the APARTMENTS.on poke, so the recovery path is NOT the discriminator here; the load is. THIS FILE IS THE SAME FRAMES RE-MEASURED WITH --from AFTER THE FIX, and nothing was re-shot: it is now exit 2, with all five A frames in verdict.uninterpretable and the five-pose verdict.loadAsymmetry beside them, and verdict.same.maskedByExitCode saying in the file that the --same failure is no longer what the exit code reports. Absolute paths rewritten; nothing else changed."
